infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why a sorted set beats a SQL table for ranks
  compares
    - label SQL table + score index
      children
        - label Top-k
          desc ORDER BY score LIMIT 10 — O(log n + k), fine
        - label My rank
          desc COUNT(*) WHERE score > mine — O(n) scan per query
        - label Update
          desc INSERT/UPDATE + index maintenance — O(log n)
    - label Redis ZSET (skip list)
      children
        - label Top-k
          desc ZREVRANGE 0 9 — O(log n + k)
        - label My rank
          desc ZREVRANK — O(log n), rank held in skip-list spans
        - label Update
          desc ZADD — O(log n) insert or reposition
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
end
